{"id":"69f749a4a722dfbc53a7a8d56fdf1fde022ddcca","axis":"silent","repo":"phan/phan","sha":"69f749a4a722dfbc53a7a8d56fdf1fde022ddcca","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"NEWS.md","lines":["@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@ New features:"," Performance improvements:"," - Reduce analysis overhead without changing the emitted issues: FQSEN and `Type` memoization no longer allocate a closure per lookup, `FullyQualifiedClassName::fromType()` is cached per type, `UnionType` string conversion and equality checks are faster for small type sets, whether a file is excluded from analysis is cached per path (and issues in excluded files are no longer formatted before being discarded), the `clone` AST normalization pass is skipped for files that do not contain `clone`, and redundant `realpath()`/stat calls were removed."," - Reduce the cost of inherited methods in the class and method analysis phases (large on projects with many inherited methods) without changing the emitted issues: resolving `static` in a union type returns immediately when none of its types can change (no `Context` is created), finding the methods that a method overrides does one lookup per ancestor class instead of three and no longer creates a method FQSEN per ancestor, an ancestor's template parameter type map is fetched once per ancestor instead of once per inherited method, and creating method/property/class constant FQSENs no longer builds a string cache key (or lowercases method names that cannot be magic methods).","+- Speed up the parse phase without changing the emitted issues: no `ParseVisitor` is created for nodes of the 88 kinds whose handler only returns the current context (most nodes; a unit test checks the list against the handlers of `ParseVisitor`), the AST simplifier no longer checks the elements of an array literal for side effects when none of them would be trimmed and no longer creates an array per node it visits, doc comments without a multi-line annotation skip the multi-line reduction, finding the line of a `@param`/`@return` tag splits the file with `explode()` instead of `preg_split()` (the doc comment lines contain no newlines, so the comparisons are the same) and reuses the absolute path of the file, types without template parameters no longer create a closure, and the check that a file to parse still exists uses `file_exists()` instead of `realpath()`. This makes the parse phase about 12 % faster on a large project."," - Skip the checks that only emit issues about the declaration of a function or method (the order of `@param` tags, promotion modifiers, required parameters after optional ones, impossible types without intersection types, default values, `@override`/`@inheritDoc` comments) when it is declared in a file excluded from analysis, such as `vendor/`, including the methods that classes inherit from those files. Phan discarded those issues anyway. The steps that the rest of the analysis depends on still run: scope initialization, phpdoc type narrowing and inheritance, return type inference, inherited `@throws` types, attributes, duplicate definition checks, the plugins' `analyzeFunction`/`analyzeMethod`, the signature compatibility checks against overridden methods and the impossible-combination checks of intersection types (both expand types, which hydrates classes), and the lookups of the classes used in parameter, return and `@throws` types, which load internal classes (for parameter and return types of these elements, they now run once per type instead of once per function or method). This makes the method analysis phase about 8 % faster on a large project where most methods are declared in excluded files, without changing the issues reported. Set `PHAN_ANALYZE_EXCLUDED_METHODS=1` to run the checks anyway. `PHAN_VERIFY_SKIPPED_CHECKS=1` runs them and exits with an error if any of them emitted an issue in an analyzed file, modified the function or method, or threw. `PHAN_DUMP_METHOD_STATE_DIGEST=<path>` writes the types and flags of every user-defined function and method and the order in which internal methods were loaded when the analysis phase starts, to compare runs with and without `PHAN_ANALYZE_EXCLUDED_METHODS=1`."," - Skip two walks over the methods that an inherited method overrides when they cannot find anything, without changing the emitted issues: the search for an inherited `@phan-mandatory-param` when no method with the same name has a parameter marked `@phan-mandatory-param`, and the search for inherited `@throws` types when no method with the same name declares `@throws`. This is never done for `__construct` (default constructors are created lazily), and not at all once a class was hydrated while the hydration of one of its ancestors was unfinished (e.g. an inheritance cycle). `PHAN_VERIFY_SKIPPED_CHECKS=1` also runs these walks and exits with an error if one of them found something, initialized the scope of a user-defined method, hydrated a class or threw, or if the overridden methods of a method whose walks were skipped changed by the end of the method analysis phase. Also, the checks for references to classes that are declared more than once no longer look up a second declaration of classes declared once, and finding the parameters that take callables or class names (for the internal callable checks and `AnalyzeCallableArgumentCapability` plugins) no longer allocates two closures per parameter. On a large project with about 640,000 inherited methods, this makes the method analysis phase about 5 % faster (18.7 s -> 17.8 s), the plugin loading step about 15 % faster and the whole run about 2 % faster at `-j 1`."," "],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Phan/AST/ASTSimplifier.php","lines":["@@ -414,15 +414,18 @@ private static function trimArrayNode(Node $array_node, int $budget): array","         $allowed = min($budget, self::getTrimMaxElementsPerLevel(), $total);","         $indexes = self::selectRepresentativeIndexes($total, $allowed);"," ","-        $side_effect_indexes = [];","-        foreach ($children as $index => $child) {","-            if ($child instanceof Node && self::arrayElementHasPossibleSideEffects($child)) {","-                $side_effect_indexes[] = $index;","+        // When every element is kept ($allowed === $total), adding the elements with side effects changes nothing.","+        if ($allowed < $total) {","+            $side_effect_indexes = [];","+            foreach ($children as $index => $child) {","+                if ($child instanceof Node && self::arrayElementHasPossibleSideEffects($child)) {","+                    $side_effect_indexes[] = $index;","+                }","+            }","+            if ($side_effect_indexes) {","+                $indexes = array_values(array_unique(array_merge($indexes, $side_effect_indexes)));","+                sort($indexes, SORT_NUMERIC);","             }","-        }","-        if ($side_effect_indexes) {","-            $indexes = array_values(array_unique(array_merge($indexes, $side_effect_indexes)));","-            sort($indexes, SORT_NUMERIC);","         }"," ","         $extra_budget = max(0, $budget - count($indexes));","@@ -625,24 +628,36 @@ private static function distributeBudget(int $budget, int $count): array","     }"," ","     /**","-     * @return array{0:Node,1:bool}","+     * @return array{0:Node,1:bool} the node with the arrays in its descendants trimmed (or $node), and whether any array was trimmed","      */","     private static function trimDescendantArrays(Node $node): array","+    {","+        $trimmed = false;","+        $new_node = self::trimDescendantArraysInner($node, $trimmed);","+        return [$new_node, $trimmed];","+    }","+","+    /**","+     * The implementation of trimDescendantArrays(), which is called on most nodes of expressions.","+     * (This avoids creating an array for the result of each recursive call)","+     *","+     * @param bool $trimmed set to true if any array was trimmed (never set to false)","+     */","+    private static function trimDescendantArraysInner(Node $node, bool &$trimmed): Node","     {","         $children = $node->children;","         $modified = false;","-        $trimmed = false;","         foreach ($children as $key => $child) {","             if (!($child instanceof Node)) {","                 continue;","             }","             if ($child->kind === ast\\AST_ARRAY) {","                 [$new_child, , $child_trimmed] = self::trimArrayNode($child, self::getTrimMaxTotalElements());","+                if ($child_trimmed) {","+                    $trimmed = true;","+                }","             } else {","-                [$new_child, $child_trimmed] = self::trimDescendantArrays($child);","-            }","-            if ($child_trimmed) {","-                $trimmed = true;","+                $new_child = self::trimDescendantArraysInner($child, $trimmed);","             }","             if ($new_child !== $child) {","                 if (!$modified) {","@@ -653,11 +668,11 @@ private static function trimDescendantArrays(Node $node): array","             }","         }","         if (!$modified) {","-            return [$node, $trimmed];","+            return $node;","         }","         $clone = clone($node);","         $clone->children = $children;","-        return [$clone, $trimmed];","+        return $clone;","     }"," ","     /**"],"additions":31,"deletions":16,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Phan/Analysis.php","lines":["@@ -442,6 +442,18 @@ public static function parseNodeInContext(CodeBase $code_base, Context $context,","         $kind = $node->kind;","         $context->setLineNumberStart($node->lineno);"," ","+        if (isset(ParseVisitor::NO_OP_NODE_KINDS[$kind])) {","+            // ParseVisitor's handler for this kind (most nodes) returns $context and does nothing else,","+            // so skip creating the visitor. This is equivalent to the default case below.","+            $child_context = $context;","+            foreach ($node->children as $child_node) {","+                if (\\is_object($child_node)) {","+                    $child_context = self::parseNodeInContext($code_base, $child_context, $child_node);","+                }","+            }","+            return $context;","+        }","+","         // Visit the given node populating the code base","         // with anything we learn and get a new context","         // indicating the state of the world within the"],"additions":12,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Phan/Language/Element/Comment/Builder.php","lines":["@@ -1342,9 +1342,24 @@ private function parsePhanMethod(int $i, string $line): void","         }","     }"," ","+    /**","+     * @var array{0:string,1:string,2:string}|null [the project root directory, the file of the context, Config::projectPath() of that file]","+     * of the most recent call to guessActualLineLocation(), which is called for every (at)param and (at)return line.","+     */","+    private static $last_project_path = null;","+","     private function guessActualLineLocation(int $i): int","     {","-        $path = Config::projectPath($this->context->getFile());","+        $file = $this->context->getFile();","+        $root = Config::getProjectRootDirectory();","+        $last_project_path = self::$last_project_path;","+        if ($last_project_path !== null && $last_project_path[1] === $file && $last_project_path[0] === $root) {","+            $path = $last_project_path[2];","+        } else {","+            // Config::projectPath() is a pure function of the project root directory and the file","+            $path = Config::projectPath($file);","+            self::$last_project_path = [$root, $file, $path];","+        }","         $entry = FileCache::getEntry($path);","         $declaration_lineno = $this->lineno;","         if (!$entry) {","@@ -1354,7 +1369,9 @@ private function guessActualLineLocation(int $i): int","         $lineno_search = $declaration_lineno - ($this->comment_lines_count - $i - 1);","         // Search up to 10 lines before $lineno_search","         $lineno_stop = \\max(1, $lineno_search - 9);","-        $lines_array = $entry->getLines();","+        // The lines of the doc comment contain no \"\\n\", so the checks below have the same result for the lines of getLines(),","+        // which end in \"\\n\", and for these lines, which are much faster to compute.","+        $lines_array = $entry->getLinesWithoutNewlines();"," ","         $line = $this->lines[$i];","         $trimmed_line = \\trim($line);","@@ -1952,6 +1969,11 @@ protected function emitDeferredIssues(): void"," ","     private static function reduceMultiline(string $comment): string","     {","+        $comment = \\str_replace(\"\\r\", '', $comment);","+        // The closure below only changes an annotation if it contains an opening bracket followed by a newline.","+        if (!str_contains($comment, \"(\\n\") && !str_contains($comment, \"[\\n\") && !str_contains($comment, \"<\\n\") && !str_contains($comment, \"{\\n\")) {","+            return $comment;","+        }","         return \\implode('@', \\array_map(","             static function (string $annotation): string {","                 if (!str_contains($annotation, \"\\n\")","@@ -1995,7 +2017,7 @@ static function (string $annotation): string {"," ","                 return $buffer;","             },","-            \\explode('@', \\str_replace(\"\\r\", '', $comment))","+            \\explode('@', $comment)","         ));","     }"," }"],"additions":25,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Phan/Language/Type.php","lines":["@@ -1554,10 +1554,11 @@ public static function fromStringInContext("," ","         // Map the names of the types to actual types in the","         // template parameter type list","-        $template_parameter_type_list =","+        // (Most types have no template parameters, so skip creating the closure for those)","+        $template_parameter_type_list = $template_parameter_type_name_list ?","             \\array_map(static function (string $type_name) use ($code_base, $context, $source): UnionType {","                 return UnionType::fromStringInContext($type_name, $context, $source, $code_base);","-            }, $template_parameter_type_name_list);","+            }, $template_parameter_type_name_list) : [];"," ","         // @var bool","         // True if this type name if of the form 'C[]'"],"additions":3,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Phan/Library/FileCacheEntry.php","lines":["@@ -36,6 +36,9 @@ class FileCacheEntry","     /** @var ?associative-array<int,string> a 1-based array of lines */","     private $lines;"," ","+    /** @var ?associative-array<int,string> a 1-based array of lines without the trailing newline */","+    private $lines_without_newlines;","+","     /**","      * Create a representation of the file contents.","      *","@@ -147,6 +150,24 @@ public function getLines(): array","         return $lines;","     }"," ","+    /**","+     * Like getLines(), but without the \"\\n\" at the end of each line (which is much faster to compute).","+     * If the contents end with \"\\n\", this has an additional empty last line.","+     *","+     * @return associative-array<int,string> a 1-based array of lines","+     */","+    public function getLinesWithoutNewlines(): array","+    {","+        if (\\is_array($this->lines_without_newlines)) {","+            return $this->lines_without_newlines;","+        }","+        $lines = \\explode(\"\\n\", $this->contents);","+        \\array_unshift($lines, '');","+        unset($lines[0]);","+        $this->lines_without_newlines = $lines;","+        return $lines;","+    }","+"," ","     /**","      * Helper method to get individual lines from a file."],"additions":21,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Phan/Parse/ParseVisitor.php","lines":["@@ -2112,6 +2112,104 @@ public function visitNamespace(Node $node): Context","         return parent::visitNamespace($node);","     }"," ","+    /**","+     * The node kinds for which the handler of ParseVisitor returns $this->context and has no side effects","+     * (the inherited KindVisitorImplementation methods that call ScopeVisitor::visit(), and the no-ops below).","+     *","+     * Analysis::parseNodeInContext() does not create a ParseVisitor for nodes of these kinds.","+     * This must be updated when a handler for one of these kinds is added or changed (ParseVisitorNoOpKindsTest checks this).","+     */","+    public const NO_OP_NODE_KINDS = [","+        ast\\AST_ARG_LIST => true,","+        ast\\AST_ARRAY => true,","+        ast\\AST_ARRAY_ELEM => true,","+        ast\\AST_ASSIGN => true,","+        ast\\AST_ASSIGN_OP => true,","+        ast\\AST_ASSIGN_REF => true,","+        ast\\AST_ATTRIBUTE => true,","+        ast\\AST_ATTRIBUTE_LIST => true,","+        ast\\AST_ATTRIBUTE_GROUP => true,","+        ast\\AST_BINARY_OP => true,","+        ast\\AST_BREAK => true,","+        ast\\AST_CALLABLE_CONVERT => true,","+        ast\\AST_CAST => true,","+        ast\\AST_CATCH => true,","+        ast\\AST_CLASS_CONST => true,","+        ast\\AST_CLASS_CONST_DECL => true,","+        ast\\AST_CLASS_NAME => true,","+        ast\\AST_CLOSURE_USES => true,","+        ast\\AST_CLOSURE_VAR => true,","+        ast\\AST_CONST => true,","+        ast\\AST_CONST_ELEM => true,","+        ast\\AST_DIM => true,","+        ast\\AST_DO_WHILE => true,","+        ast\\AST_ECHO => true,","+        ast\\AST_EMPTY => true,","+        ast\\AST_ENCAPS_LIST => true,","+        ast\\AST_EXIT => true,","+        ast\\AST_EXPR_LIST => true,","+        ast\\AST_FOREACH => true,","+        ast\\AST_ISSET => true,","+        ast\\AST_GLOBAL => true,","+        ast\\AST_IF => true,","+        ast\\AST_IF_ELEM => true,","+        ast\\AST_INSTANCEOF => true,","+        ast\\AST_MAGIC_CONST => true,","+        ast\\AST_MATCH => true,","+        ast\\AST_MATCH_ARM => true,","+        ast\\AST_MATCH_ARM_LIST => true,","